 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Lots of small steps really. Shorter desk chair, get up regularly, and mix up sitting and kneeling with standing. A stool is great for floor time. Try sitting on an easy chair footstool. Most people find one inch to two inches gives full height back without feeling too wide. Not necessarily, an ergonomist would tell you to alternate between several chairs with one about inch too short, so you move along them. Then try sitting on a cushion across several chair inches while you' working. It lifts you without making a big change.",
